From 4475a083a6e8acc0dc36004644c03043a63d1e6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chen Xiaohui <graych@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 3 May 2026 22:04:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] vmm: hand off in-process MISSING userfaultfd to the
 external owner

Keep uffd_socket configuration, parser and Landlock permissions with in-process UFFD creation, registration, SCM_RIGHTS handoff and the legacy acknowledgement. The CH address space owns fault registration; its external peer owns fault service.

Reorganized from original patch 0003 and the socket configuration formerly carried by 0001. No new capability or dirty-memory protocol is introduced.

Signed-off-by: Chen Xiaohui <graych@gmail.com>
